  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe SVG reader, `camcraft_geometry::svg`, reads drawings into the DXF `Document` type. It shares sketch chaining, nesting, `SketchData`, sketch entities, and project storage with DXF import.\n\n- Read paths, lines, polylines, polygons, rectangles, circles, and ellipses.\n- Apply group transforms and references to elements in the same file.\n- Keep circular arcs analytic. Flatten Beziers and other ellipses within 0.005 mm.\n- Read mm, cm, in, pt, pc, and px sizes, `viewBox`, and `preserveAspectRatio`.\n- Reflect Y about the page height. Use top-level group labels or IDs as layers.\n- Count unsupported content, hidden content, and stylesheets as skipped. This includes stylesheets inside `<defs>`.\n- Add the undoable `ImportSvg` command, the `import_svg` MCP tool, and the `cam.importSvg` script verb.\n- Update the user guide and MCP reference. Record decisions in `docs/decisions/1880-svg-import.md`.\n\n## Refusals\n\nThe reader names malformed input, unsupported units, invalid sizes, singular transforms, and exceeded import limits. A file without physical units needs the caller's unit. A sized file refuses a caller unit.\n\nThe reader also refuses inline CSS `transform` declarations and root `<svg>` transform attributes.\n\nThis review fix refuses `transform-origin` presentation attributes and inline CSS declarations by name before drawing geometry. Pins cover both sources.\n\n## Validation on the final head\n\nHead: `ad6709150d06595bc5b347a651702854681f457c`.\nBase at gate launch: `upstream/main`, `6e641dac753020bfed49fec310237eed28448141`.\nUpstream advanced during the run to `64b7377297c95d1614c93835c1a1bef18c6de174`.\nThe gates tested the final PR head. They did not test a trial merge.\nA merge-tree check with the newer upstream head is clean.\nSelection comparison against the newer base: the old and current bases have the same merge base, `6e1805bfdae52fcfea71a946d381dfbfdefc79f5`. Quick (1,067 steps) and heavy (241 steps) select identical step names and commands against both bases. The final source and selection are unchanged, so no rerun was required.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1 CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1 cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` | PASS: 1,067 steps, zero failures, 40.8 minutes |\n| `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1 CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1 cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` | PASS: 241 steps, zero failures, 65.1 minutes |\n| `cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` | PASS in the final quick gate; all targets with `-D warnings`, including geometry, app, and six other crates |\n| `app suites: example_catalog` | `app suites: example_catalog` in the final quick gate: 33 passed, 2 ignored; adaptive and edgework catalog suites: 1 passed each |\n| SVG suites and other reached golden suites | SVG: 15 passed; refusals: 16 passed; visibility: 11 passed. Total: 42 passed. Reached catalog suites passed |\n\nPin proof:\n\n- `svg_transform_origin_attribute_is_refused_by_name`: removing the attribute guard failed the exact pin at its assertion (exit 101); restoring the guard passed the pin (1 passed).\n- `svg_inline_css_transform_origin_is_refused_by_name`: removing the inline guard failed the exact pin at its assertion (exit 101); restoring the guard passed the pin (1 passed).\n\nEach mutation removed the relevant refusal, failed the pin, restored the refusal, and passed the pin.\n\nAn earlier seeded run failed with an infrastructure error (`E0463`) in the kernel artifact cache. A targeted repair restored the cache. The final quick gate above passed without seed artifacts.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The catalog suites passed. No recorded program or golden changed, so no regeneration was required.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A posted G-code golden for an SVG profile remains in follow-up #3042. This fix round did not exercise it.\n- The `import_svg` row in `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` remains outside this fix round.\n- Nested SVG viewports, stylesheet evaluation, text to outlines, and embedded images remain outside this reader's scope.\n\nNo UI source changed. Before/after screenshots do not apply.\n\nChangelog: Import SVG drawings (paths, shapes, group transforms, mm/cm/in/pt/pc/px sizes) as 2D profiles on the stock, with the `import_svg` MCP tool and `cam.importSvg`; an SVG with no physical size is refused until you state its unit.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1880\n",
